ada, Mexico, New Zealand, and Italy. It offers beer under the Corona Extra, Corona Familiar, Corona Sunbrew, Corona Light, Corona Non-Alcoholic, Corona Premier, Modelo Especial, Modelo Chelada, Modelo Negra, Modelo Spiked Aguas Frescas, Modelo Oro, Modelo Noche Especial, Victoria, Vicky Chamoy, and Pacifico brand names. The company also offers wine under the Sea Smoke, Schrader Cellars, Kim Crawford, Mount Veeder, Ruffino, My Favorite Neighbor, Robert Mondavi Winery, and The Prisoner Wine Company brand names; and spirits under the Casa Noble, High West, Mi CAMPO, and Nelson's Green Brier brand names. Additionally, it offers a spirit-based, ready-to-drink alcoholic beverage under the SpikedAde brand. It provides its products to wholesale distributors, retailers, and state alcohol beverage control agencies. Constellation Brands, Inc. was founded in 1945 and is headquartered in Rochester, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Nicholas Ian Fink J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $118,173 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $191K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Constellation Brands, Inc. is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $24.0B market cap on $9.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.58\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 7.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 3.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 35% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Constellation Brands (STZ) Beats On Beer, Is 5% Undervalued Enough?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/constellation-brands-stz-beats-beer-032018569.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793935218.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Did Constellation Brands (NYSE:STZ) Maintain Its Annual Guidance?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/why-did-constellation-brands-nysestz-maintain-its-annual-guidance","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793900820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Constellation Brands (STZ) Up 22.9% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024573/constellation-brands-stz-up-22-9-since-last-earnings-report-can-it-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3024573","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793892602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Constellation Brands Inc $STZ Stake Lifted by Pzena Investment Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.co